ngage with  their consumers  bait media mobile apps and blogs  and how to be effective at it the book  also focuses on leveraging the strengths  of social media  apps and blogs to capture more leads for  less money  like i mentioned earlier the main focus  in this book  is to convert more internet leads into  real world prospects  and sales appointments let's now talk  about chris smith  he's a best-selling author and  co-founder of a blog called curator  which is a social media  digital marketing and coaching company  his work has been featured in a number  of major publications  like adweek and forbes he's also an  in-demand keynote speaker  and is often on real estate industry  lists  as one of the most influential people  within the industry  next up number nine designing brand  entity by alina wheeler  called a comprehensive pragmatic and  easy to understand  resource for brand builders by the  global brand leader of deloitte  this book mainly focuses on the  fundamentals  processes and case studies behind  creating a brand  it covers more than 100 branding  subjects  checklists tools and diagrams  the book also acts as a compendium for  tools  that can make the branding process a  success and some of the best practices  that will get you some inspiration  the book also has 50 case studies  describing goals  processes strategies solutions  and results now  let's talk about the author alina  wheeler alina wheeler is a prominent  speaker who guides teams  with everything brand related from brand  fundamentals  processes best practices and much more  she's also been coaching business  leaders and design consultancies  and has worked with more than 100  companies within the private  and public sector now let's go to number  eight  get scrappy by nick westgard called a  digital marketing bible by publishers  weekly  this book helps smaller companies with  lesser resources  to develop powerhouse results it also  aims to help  teams to think like underdogs and to  lev