 industry leader  it explains strategies that can capture  a large market share  and to build their strategies around the  competitors weaknesses  the book also helps to analyze and  incorporate  data from trends now let's talk about  already and jack trout already is an  author and marketing professional  credited with  resurrecting the idea of positioning in  marketing  jack trout was a marketer who was one of  the founders and pioneers  of marketing warfare theory and  positioning theory  next for number five epic content  marketing by joe polizzi  this book called one of fortune  magazine's top five business book  must reads explains how to attract  customers and lead them to your  businesses  by creating relevant content the book  helps determine what your brand's  content  niche is and what you need to do to keep  their  attention the book can help discover  and develop your content marketing  mission statement  and to set up a process to create and  curate  content it also explains how to leverage  social media and email channels to  create  and grow your audience now  let's talk about joe polizzi he's an  author  and an authority when it comes to  content marketing  he founded the content marketing  institute and launched  several events one among them being  content marketing  world he also won the 2014  john caldwell lifetime achievement award  by the content council  next up we have number four crushing it  by gary vaynerhook  a new york times bestseller this book  helps people build a personal brand  and how to achieve their goals the book  explains the many ways  social media platforms can be taken  advantage of  by organizations to make a personal  brand for themselves  it provides tricks and tweaks to enhance  these strategies  it also provides tactical and  theoretical advice  on how to become a star on social media  and podcast services it also details  examples from real life scenarios and  how they were handled  let's talk about gary vinhoek he's 